WEBVTT

00:03:59.329 --> 00:04:02.579
to be the source of something
as big as big data.

00:04:02.621 --> 00:04:05.371
But the way we study
the fundamental particles,

00:04:05.413 --> 00:04:07.538
as well as the forces
by which they interact,

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:09.746
involves creating them fleetingly,

00:04:09.788 --> 00:04:12.746
colliding protons in our accelerators

00:04:12.788 --> 00:04:16.454
and capturing a trace of them
as they zoom off near light speed.

00:04:16.496 --> 00:04:17.538
To see those traces,

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:22.163
our detector, with 150 million sensors,
acts like a really massive 3-D camera,

00:04:22.204 --> 00:04:26.788
taking a picture of each collision event -
that’s up to 14 million times per second.

00:04:26.829 --> 00:04:28.204
That makes a lot of data.

00:04:28.246 --> 00:04:30.621
But if big data 
has been around for so long,